The CIS Critical Security Controls
----------------------------------

src/cis_controls/schema/*.yaml, src/cis_controls/datamodel/ and project/
model the structure of the CIS Critical Security Controls (CIS Controls),
Version 8.1, as the Center for Internet Security, Inc. (CIS) revised it in
March 2025, when the guide's pages were labelled v8.1.2:
https://www.cisecurity.org/controls/v8-1, read on 2026-10-30. They are
this project's work, written in its own words. They are not CIS's, and
their use does not imply endorsement by CIS. CIS Critical Security
Controls and CIS Controls are registered trademarks of CIS, named here
only to say which framework is modelled.

CIS licenses the CIS Controls under the Creative Commons
Attribution-NonCommercial-NoDerivatives 4.0 International licence
(CC BY-NC-ND 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/).
That licence lets anyone copy and share CIS's guide unchanged, for
non-commercial purposes, with credit to CIS and a link to the licence. It
does not let anyone share a changed or adapted version, and CIS requires
its prior approval for any commercial use. So this repository carries no
CIS text: no Control or Safeguard title or description, and none of the
guide's overviews, explanations or procedures. It names each Control and
Safeguard by its number and records only the structure the guide sets
out: which Safeguards belong to which Control, and each Safeguard's asset
class, security function and Implementation Groups.

The schema's text slots, such as title and description, are optional and
hold whatever their user writes into them. Fill them only with text you
have the right to use: your own words, or CIS's text under CIS's licence
and any approval CIS has given you. The Apache License of this repository
does not cover CIS's text.

